From d274e1046c12457452dcc212cd8941cca17d880e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mminin <mminin2010@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 14:57:48 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Add an engine for dynamic XFA forms

Dynamic XFA forms (NeedsRendering true) only contain a "please use Adobe
Reader" page: their real pages have to be generated from the XFA template
by the viewer. XFAForm does that:

 - builds the form DOM from the template, with repeatable subforms and
   instance managers
 - runs the JavaScript of the form with QuickJS (optional dependency,
   ENABLE_XFA_SCRIPTING): an XFA object model written in JavaScript on top
   of a few native functions, SOM resolution, script objects, events,
   calculations and validations
 - lays the form out on pages: positioned, top-to-bottom and
   left-to-right layouts, page areas, breaks, splitting of flowed
   content and of long text across pages, master page objects
 - writes the result as a regular PDF with AcroForm fields, which the
   rest of poppler can render, edit and print

pdfxfa converts XFA forms to regular PDF files with it, optionally
filling in fields and clicking buttons first.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
